course: dictionary
lesson: 15177
title: A word from the river
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A sculler is a person who rows a boat with two oars, one in each hand. Those oars are called sculls, so sculling means rowing this way. «The Water Rat sculled his little boat smoothly down the river.» The clue is the two oars, one in each hand, and that is what sculling means.
explain: A sculler can also be a small, light rowing boat made for sculling. «The sculler was light and fast, so it zipped past the other boats.» Light and fast are clues that this sculler is a boat built for speed. Check by swapping in your meaning: a rower or a boat both make sense here.
explain: Sculling looks easy, but it takes practice. «Mole's first try at sculling ended with a splash in the river.» The splash is the clue: Mole is a beginner, so a sculler is someone who has learned to row this way well.
fact: A sculler rows a boat with two oars, one in each hand.
fact: «Sculls» are the oars a sculler uses.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the Water Rat is a skilled sculler, and Mole longs to learn.
fact: Scullers race on rivers such as the Thames, and sculling is an Olympic sport with single sculls and double sculls.
fact: Safety first: anyone in a rowing boat should wear a life jacket and never stand up suddenly.
exercise: «The Water Rat sculled his little boat down the river.» What is a sculler? | A bird that swims on lakes | A fish that lives in rivers | A heavy anchor for a boat | *A person who rows with two oars, one in each hand
exercise: «Mole's first try at sculling ended with him tipping the boat over.» What does sculling mean here? | Painting a boat bright colours | Swimming under the water | Sleeping on the river bank | *Rowing a boat with two oars, one in each hand
exercise: «A sculler uses two sculls, one in each hand.» Find and copy the word that means the oars. | boat | *sculls | hand | rowing
test: «A single sculler races alone in a light boat.» What does a single sculler do? | *Rows alone with two oars | Sails with a big white sail | Carries the boat on his back | Swims in a pool
test: Why should you wear a life jacket in a rowing boat? | Because it makes the boat go faster | Because it keeps you warm and dry in the sun | *Because a sudden fall in the water can be dangerous | Because it is a rule for fashion
exam: In «The sculler won the race on the Thames», which meaning fits sculler best? | *A person who rows a boat with two oars, one in each hand | A bird that dives for fish | Someone who sings on a boat | Someone who builds bridges
